            "title": "The Winners and Losers From Trump\u2019s 25% Truck Tariffs",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "\u201cOur Great Large Truck Company Manufacturers, such as Peterbilt, Kenworth, Freightliner, Mack Trucks, and others, will be protected from the onslaught of outside interruptions,\u201d wrote President Trump Thursday evening when he announced a 25% tariff on heavy trucks.  In fact, a key target of the new tax appears to be one of the brands the president said he wants to protect: Freightliner, which is owned by Germany\u2019s Daimler Trucks and assembles most of its vehicles in Mexico.  Shares in Volkswagen\u2019s truck subsidiary Traton, which makes international trucks almost exclusively in Mexico, fell 2.5%.",
